---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import CalmBackground from '../../components/CalmBackground.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout
  title="Hobby Tracker Privacy Policy — Quiet Tools"
  description="Privacy information for the Hobby Tracker app from Quiet Tools."
  canonicalPath="/hobby-tracker/privacy/"
  image="assets/hobby-tracker/hobby-tracker-app-icon.png"
>
  <CalmBackground />
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Hobby Tracker</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Hobby Tracker is designed to keep your hobby records private.</strong> It does not require an account and does not use advertising or behavioral analytics.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: August 14, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="info-grid">
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Information you add</h2>
      <p>Hobby Tracker stores the hobby details, activities, notes, measurements, photos, projects, and other content you choose to enter. This information is used to provide the app’s features.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Local storage</h2>
      <p>Your Hobby Tracker data is stored locally on your device. The app works offline and does not require you to create an account or send your hobby records to Quiet Tools.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Photos and sharing</h2>
      <p>Photos you add remain part of your local app data. They are included in a recap, export, or other shared item only when you choose to include or share them.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Exports and device backups</h2>
      <p>When you export, save, print, or share content, the destination you select may receive that content. Data on your device may also be included in device backups according to your Apple device and service settings.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>Hobby Tracker does not include third-party advertising SDKs, behavioral tracking, or app analytics used by Quiet Tools to profile your activity.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card">
      <h2>Support messages</h2>
      <p>If you contact support, Quiet Tools receives the information you choose to send, such as your email address, device details, screenshots, and issue description. Messages sent through the website support form are processed by FormSubmit and delivered to Quiet Tools by email. Please do not send private hobby records or other sensitive information.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="info-card full-width">
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>This policy may be updated if Hobby Tracker’s features or privacy practices change. The current version will remain available at this URL.</p>
      <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:support@quiettoolsapps.com?subject=Hobby%20Tracker%20Privacy">support@quiettoolsapps.com</a>.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}hobby-tracker/`}>Return to Hobby Tracker</a> · <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Quiet Tools privacy overview</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .updated { margin-top: .8rem; font-size: .95rem !important; }
  .full-width { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .info-card p + p { margin-top: .75rem; }
</style>
